# PaceSet Frontend UI Consistency

Before inventing a new control, reuse existing components. Same action = same component.

## Delete / remove

- **Always** use `DeleteIconButton` (red trash icon) — never a full-width red/outline text button for delete.
- **Always** confirm with `ConfirmDialog` before destructive API calls.
- Place the trash icon on the card/row (same pattern as Programs list).

```tsx
import { DeleteIconButton } from "@/components/DeleteIconButton";
import { ConfirmDialog } from "@/components/ConfirmDialog";
```

## Shared building blocks

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Page chrome + bottom tabs | `PhoneShell` (`showNav` when needed) |
| Title / subtitle | `PageHeader` |
| Scrollable body padding | `PageContent` |
| Delete affordance | `DeleteIconButton` |
| Confirm delete / leave / save | `ConfirmDialog` |
| Language toggle | `LanguageSwitcher` (`compact` on welcome) |
| App version label | `APP_VERSION` from `@/lib/appVersion` |

## Do not

- Create one-off delete buttons (big red text, grey bordered danger buttons).
- Skip confirm dialogs for delete/remove of user data.
- Duplicate dialog markup — extend `ConfirmDialog` if needed.

## When adding a new screen

1. Check `prese-set-fn/src/components/` for an existing pattern.
2. Match Programs / Schedule / Profile spacing and button hierarchy (primary = lime full-width; danger = trash icon only).
3. If you must invent UI, add or update a shared component first, then use it in the page.
